WARNING: This update is meant for new players or players who want to start a fresh run. It mostly changes Map01 to make it more accessible based on the feedback I've received after this first release week. Remember that updating the game ruins your previous saved games, so think twice before you do it (also, the next big update will contain new stuff to warrant a replay, so wait until then if you've already completed Map01).
General changelog & how to update here.


Thanks to everyone who has given feedback, reviews and bug reports so far! Here's what this update does more specifically:

Map01:
- Tutorial tips overhaul to make them more compact and on point;
- Item placement modification to reduce certain confusion;
- Broken switch to the Mining Outpost has been moved to the elevator in front, to make it easier to remember and see when backtracking;
- Added few new props to act as visual landmarks in the cave;
- The door next to the Iron Key has been modified to look less like something the key would open, and reduce confusion again;
- The path between the Water Cave and Dura's Office is now open from the get go - this will allow the player to loop back if they decide to explore after obtaining the Power Core, and reduce the apparent importance of the waterfall gate's crystal device;
- After obtaining the second Power Crystal, Crawlers break the shutter and enter the Mining Outpost, signalling the way towards the exit;
- Initiates now appear in the later half of the map on all difficulties;

